# DESIGN.md, File dialogs. THE ASSERTION GOES ALL THE WAY TO THE BYTES:
# nothing asserts that a dialog closed, so the status lines fail unless
# a real descriptor came back carrying the real file. What this scene
# uniquely proves is that the capability SURVIVES CROSSING A THREAD (a
# security-scoped URL on iOS, a content:// URI plus a JNI reference on
# Android). The file is the guest's own, named by BASENAME only.
expect label#0 "no file"

# ARM THE DIRECTORY FIRST: NSOpenPanel honors `directoryURL` only when
# it is PRESENTED — set on an open panel it is ignored, and the panel
# restores whatever location it used last.
file_dialog_goto $TMP/kaya-picked-$PID
click button#0

# TWO FILES, and the one that sorts FIRST is not the one to pick: a
# dialog completes with the only row when nothing is selected, so a
# single-file directory lets `file_choose` pass having selected nothing
# (measured on GTK), and the decoy's contents differ so a wrong pick
# fails the bytes too. The panel is read back from the PLATFORM: one
# pointed elsewhere, or filtered to nothing, presents perfectly.
expect_file_dialog kaya-picked-$PID decoy.txt picked.txt

file_choose picked.txt

# THE HANDLER RETURNED WITHOUT READING: a guest that read inline arrives
# here already showing the final text and fails.
expect label#0 "reading"

# THE CLAIM: the app thread must still serve input while a read is
# outstanding — `PickedFile::open` blocks, and a cloud provider may
# download the file before it returns. A guest that read on the app
# thread wedges it, so this click is never processed and EVERY step
# below fails too; that cascade is the signature, and a guest that is
# merely fast cannot imitate it.
click button#2
expect label#0 "1 picked bytes"

# CANCEL IS THE EMPTY LIST — no platform can confirm an empty selection,
# so there is no sentinel — and it also proves the dialog id RETIRED,
# since a second show would panic if the first were still live.
#
# ARMED AGAIN, because a second picker inherits nothing: NSOpenPanel
# reopens where it last was and GTK opens on Recent, which has no path
# bar at all.
file_dialog_goto $TMP/kaya-picked-$PID
click button#1
expect_file_dialog kaya-picked-$PID decoy.txt picked.txt
file_choose cancel
expect label#0 "cancelled"

# One REAL-TREE read at the end: everything above reads kaya's own model
# and would pass for an arm that ran and drew nothing.
expect_ax label#0 "label/cancelled"
